# Quit: the computer restarts (asked once more), and the program starts again
# from the AUTO folder: a run leaves nothing behind that the next trips on.
@twice
# A restart makes TOS 3.06 size and test the memory itself (Hatari's own start
# skips that), and Hatari's TT with no TT-RAM answers its probe and then
# faults its test, so the CPU halts: the TT's restart is the machine's to show.
@skip tt-306 -- Hatari's TT halts in TOS 3.06's own memory test
say "^Press a key" 100
key x
key q
key q
sayn 2 "^SidecarTridge" boot
sayn 2 "^Press a key" 1500
